### 4.0 Requirement → implementation map

| Required behaviour | Implementation (step name in the file) |
|---|---|
| 1. Reject non-owner actors | *Verify the triggering actor is the repository owner* — `github.actor` vs `github.repository_owner`, case-insensitive; repeated in Job B |
| 2. Reject dispatch from a branch other than `main` | *Verify the dispatch ref is main* — `github.ref_type == "branch"` **and** `github.ref == "refs/heads/main"`; repeated in Job B |
| 3. Validate the full SHA format | *Validate the supplied commit SHA* — regex `^[0-9a-f]{40}$` |
| 4. Fetch the required Git history | `actions/checkout@v7` with `ref: <sha>`, `fetch-depth: 0`, `persist-credentials: false`, plus `git fetch --no-tags origin main` |
| 5. Verify SHA reachable from `origin/main` | *Verify the commit is an ancestor of origin/main* — `git merge-base --is-ancestor` (Job A and Job B) |
| 6. Verify CI status for that exact SHA | *Verify CI status for the exact commit* — `gh api repos/{repo}/actions/runs?head_sha=$SHA`, filtered to `.github/workflows/ci.yaml`, latest run must be `success` |
| 7. Check out the exact SHA | `ref:` is the SHA in both jobs (never a moving branch name) |
| 8. Set up Node/pnpm | `pnpm/action-setup@v4` (9.15.9 = `packageManager` in package.json) + `actions/setup-node@v7`; Job A → Node 22 (matches `ci.yaml`), Job B → Node 26.x (matches the Vercel project `nodeVersion: "26.x"`; Node 26.0–26.13 confirmed present in `actions/node-versions`) |
| 9. Frozen-lockfile install | `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` (lockfile verified in sync: `--frozen-lockfile --lockfile-only` exits 0 and leaves `pnpm-lock.yaml` unchanged) |
| 10. Test / typecheck / lint / build gates | `pnpm run typecheck`, `pnpm run lint`, `pnpm run test`, `VERCEL=1 pnpm run build` in Job A (VERCEL=1 reproduces the Vercel cloud target — `vite.config.ts:226` skips the Cloudflare plugin when `process.env.VERCEL` is set, so the Node server build is produced) |
| 11. Separate job for production credentials | Job B is the only job with `environment: production` and the only job referencing `secrets.*`; Job A has `permissions: {contents: read, actions: read}` and no environment |
| 12. Deploy only to the exact project and team | *Verify the exact project and team linkage* — writes `.vercel/project.json` from the two Environment secrets, then re-reads `GET /v9/projects/{id}` and asserts `id`, `account.id` and `link.productionBranch` |
| 13. Wait for `READY` | *Wait for READY and capture the deployment id* — polls `GET /v13/deployments/{id}` every 5 s for up to 15 min; `ERROR` or timeout = failure |
| 14. Capture deployment id and URL | id from the CLI output (`dpl_[A-Za-z0-9]{25}`) with a `GET /v6/deployments` match as fallback; URL parsed from the CLI output with the project production alias `https://zes-builder.vercel.app` excluded |
| 15. Health and smoke checks on the deployment URL | *Health and smoke checks against the staged deployment URL* — `/` → 200, `/api/health` → 200 **and** body contains `"status":"healthy"`, `/api/websites` → 401 (the authenticated-boundary check) |
| 16. Clear staged summary | *Staged deployment summary* — writes the exact mandated text to `$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY` and the job output |
| Job separation | Job A `validate` (no secrets, no environment) → `needs: validate` → Job B `staged-deployment` (`environment: production`, secrets only here) |
| Pinned Vercel CLI | `VERCEL_CLI_VERSION: 65.9.0` (the version validated locally), installed with `npm install --global vercel@${VERCEL_CLI_VERSION}` — **not** `vercel@latest` |
| No automatic promotion | no `vercel promote` / `rollback` / `alias assign` / `redeploy` command exists in the file; the workflow only creates a **Staged** deployment |
| No alias movement | *Verify that production was not touched* asserts the current production deployment id is unchanged, `app.zes.codes` is still assigned to it, and the staged deployment is **not** the current production deployment; the staged deployment's own alias list must not contain `app.zes.codes` |


### 4.1 Complete proposed file (verbatim, as prepared locally)

```yaml
name: Production Release

# Single-owner production release pipeline.
#
# Barrier 1 (automatic Git deployments from main) lives in vercel.json:
#   {"git": {"deploymentEnabled": {"main": false}}}
#
# Barrier 2 (deployment creation is separated from production promotion) lives in
# the Vercel project setting "Auto-assign Custom Production Domains = false".
# Every production build created here is STAGED. This workflow never promotes.
#
# The owner is the only operator: there are no required reviewers and no
# self-review prevention. The explicit `workflow_dispatch` below IS the release
# decision, and the GitHub Environment is used only as a credentials boundary
# and as a deployment-history record.

on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      ref:
        description: 'Full 40-character commit SHA to release (must be reachable from main)'
        required: true
        type: string

permissions:
  contents: read

concurrency:
  group: production-release
  cancel-in-progress: false

env:
  VERCEL_CLI_VERSION: 65.9.0
  PRODUCTION_DOMAIN: app.zes.codes

jobs:
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Job A - Validate. No production credentials, no environment, no deployment.
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  validate:
    name: Validate release candidate
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 45
    permissions:
      contents: read
      actions: read
    outputs:
      sha: ${{ steps.validate-sha.outputs.sha }}
    steps:
      - name: Verify the triggering actor is the repository owner
        env:
          ACTOR: ${{ github.actor }}
          OWNER: ${{ github.repository_owner }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          if [ "${ACTOR,,}" != "${OWNER,,}" ]; then
            echo "::error::the release must be initiated by the repository owner (${OWNER}); actor was ${ACTOR}"
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "actor=${ACTOR} repository_owner=${OWNER}"

      - name: Verify the dispatch ref is main
        env:
          REF: ${{ github.ref }}
          REF_TYPE: ${{ github.ref_type }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          if [ "$REF_TYPE" != "branch" ]; then
            echo "::error::the workflow must be dispatched against a branch, got '${REF_TYPE}'"
            exit 1
          fi
          if [ "$REF" != "refs/heads/main" ]; then
            echo "::error::the workflow must be dispatched from main, got '${REF}'"
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "dispatch ref=${REF}"

      - name: Validate the supplied commit SHA
        id: validate-sha
        env:
          INPUT_REF: ${{ inputs.ref }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          if ! printf '%s' "$INPUT_REF" | grep -Eq '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; then
            echo "::error::the ref input must be a full 40-character lowercase commit SHA"
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "sha=$INPUT_REF" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
          echo "release candidate=$INPUT_REF"

      - name: Checkout the exact commit
        uses: actions/checkout@v7
        with:
          ref: ${{ steps.validate-sha.outputs.sha }}
          fetch-depth: 0
          persist-credentials: false

      - name: Verify the commit is an ancestor of origin/main
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          git fetch --no-tags --depth=50 origin main
          if ! git merge-base --is-ancestor "${{ steps.validate-sha.outputs.sha }}" origin/main; then
            echo "::error::the supplied SHA is not reachable from origin/main"
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "the supplied SHA is reachable from origin/main"

      - name: Verify CI status for the exact commit
        env:
          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
          SHA: ${{ steps.validate-sha.outputs.sha }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          runs=$(gh api "repos/${{ github.repository }}/actions/runs?head_sha=${SHA}&per_page=100" \
            --jq '[.workflow_runs[] | select(.path == ".github/workflows/ci.yaml")]')
          count=$(printf '%s' "$runs" | jq 'length')
          if [ "$count" -eq 0 ]; then
            echo "::error::no CI/CD workflow run was found for ${SHA}; refusing to release"
            exit 1
          fi
          latest=$(printf '%s' "$runs" | jq -r 'max_by(.created_at) | "\(.conclusion) \(.html_url)"')
          conclusion=$(printf '%s' "$runs" | jq -r 'max_by(.created_at) | .conclusion')
          if [ "$conclusion" != "success" ]; then
            echo "::error::the latest CI/CD run for ${SHA} is '${conclusion}'; refusing to release"
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "CI/CD run for ${SHA}: ${latest}"

      - name: Setup pnpm
        uses: pnpm/action-setup@v4
        with:
          version: 9.15.9
          run_install: false

      - name: Setup Node
        uses: actions/setup-node@v7
        with:
          node-version: 22
          cache: pnpm

      - name: Install dependencies
        run: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile

      - name: Typecheck
        run: pnpm run typecheck

      - name: Lint
        run: pnpm run lint

      - name: Test
        run: pnpm run test

      - name: Production build (Node server target, matching the Vercel build)
        env:
          VERCEL: '1'
        run: pnpm run build

      - name: Validation summary
        run: |
          echo "validation passed for ${{ steps.validate-sha.outputs.sha }}"

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Job B - Staged production deployment. Production credentials live here only.
  # The deployment is created as STAGED. Nothing is promoted.
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  staged-deployment:
    name: Staged production deployment (no promotion)
    needs: validate
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 45
    environment:
      name: production
    permissions:
      contents: read
      deployments: write
    env:
      VERCEL_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_TOKEN }}
      VERCEL_ORG_ID: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_ORG_ID }}
      VERCEL_PROJECT_ID: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID }}
    steps:
      - name: Mask the Vercel token
        run: echo "::add-mask::${VERCEL_TOKEN}"

      - name: Revalidate actor, dispatch ref and commit SHA
        env:
          ACTOR: ${{ github.actor }}
          OWNER: ${{ github.repository_owner }}
          REF: ${{ github.ref }}
          REF_TYPE: ${{ github.ref_type }}
          SHA: ${{ needs.validate.outputs.sha }}
          INPUT_REF: ${{ inputs.ref }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          if [ "${ACTOR,,}" != "${OWNER,,}" ]; then
            echo "::error::the release must be initiated by the repository owner (${OWNER}); actor was ${ACTOR}"
            exit 1
          fi
          if [ "$REF_TYPE" != "branch" ] || [ "$REF" != "refs/heads/main" ]; then
            echo "::error::the workflow must be dispatched from main, got '${REF}'"
            exit 1
          fi
          if ! printf '%s' "$INPUT_REF" | grep -Eq '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; then
            echo "::error::the ref input must be a full 40-character lowercase commit SHA"
            exit 1
          fi
          if [ "$INPUT_REF" != "$SHA" ]; then
            echo "::error::the validated SHA and the dispatched SHA do not match"
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "revalidated actor=${ACTOR} ref=${REF} sha=${SHA}"

      - name: Checkout the exact commit
        uses: actions/checkout@v7
        with:
          ref: ${{ needs.validate.outputs.sha }}
          fetch-depth: 0
          persist-credentials: false

      - name: Verify the commit is still an ancestor of origin/main
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          git fetch --no-tags --depth=50 origin main
          if ! git merge-base --is-ancestor "${{ needs.validate.outputs.sha }}" origin/main; then
            echo "::error::the supplied SHA is not reachable from origin/main"
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "the supplied SHA is reachable from origin/main"

      - name: Setup pnpm
        uses: pnpm/action-setup@v4
        with:
          version: 9.15.9
          run_install: false

      - name: Setup Node
        uses: actions/setup-node@v7
        with:
          node-version: 26.x
          cache: pnpm

      - name: Install dependencies
        run: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile

      - name: Install the pinned Vercel CLI
        run: npm install --global "vercel@${VERCEL_CLI_VERSION}"

      - name: Verify the CLI version and the token
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          vercel --version
          vercel whoami --token "$VERCEL_TOKEN"

      - name: Verify the exact project and team linkage
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          mkdir -p .vercel
          printf '{"projectId":"%s","orgId":"%s"}\n' "$VERCEL_PROJECT_ID" "$VERCEL_ORG_ID" > .vercel/project.json
          node --input-type=module -e "
            import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
            const link = JSON.parse(readFileSync('.vercel/project.json', 'utf8'));
            if (link.projectId !== process.env.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID) {
              console.error('project link mismatch');
              process.exit(1);
            }
            if (link.orgId !== process.env.VERCEL_ORG_ID) {
              console.error('team link mismatch');
              process.exit(1);
            }
            console.log('project link: ' + link.projectId + ' / team ' + link.orgId);
          "
          node --input-type=module -e "
            const response = await fetch('https://api.vercel.com/v9/projects/' + process.env.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID, {
              headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + process.env.VERCEL_TOKEN },
            });
            if (!response.ok) {
              console.error('the token cannot read the project');
              process.exit(1);
            }
            const project = await response.json();
            if (project.id !== process.env.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID) {
              console.error('project id mismatch');
              process.exit(1);
            }
            if (project.account?.id !== process.env.VERCEL_ORG_ID) {
              console.error('team mismatch: ' + project.account?.id);
              process.exit(1);
            }
            if (project.link?.productionBranch !== 'main') {
              console.error('unexpected production branch: ' + project.link?.productionBranch);
              process.exit(1);
            }
            console.log('verified project ' + project.id + ' (' + project.name + ') in team ' + project.account.id);
          "

      - name: Pull production project settings and environment
        run: vercel pull --yes --environment=production --token "$VERCEL_TOKEN"

      - name: Build the production artifact
        run: vercel build --prod --token "$VERCEL_TOKEN"

      - name: Record the production state before the deployment
        id: before
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          node --input-type=module -e "
            const response = await fetch('https://api.vercel.com/v9/projects/' + process.env.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID, {
              headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + process.env.VERCEL_TOKEN },
            });
            const project = await response.json();
            const production = project.targets?.production ?? {};
            const aliases = (production.alias ?? []).join(',');
            console.log('current production deployment: ' + production.id);
            console.log('current production aliases: ' + aliases);
            console.log('autoAssignCustomDomains: ' + project.autoAssignCustomDomains);
            if (!production.id) {
              console.error('no current production deployment found');
              process.exit(1);
            }
            const fs = await import('node:fs');
            fs.appendFileSync(process.env.GITHUB_OUTPUT, 'production_id=' + production.id + '\n');
            fs.appendFileSync(process.env.GITHUB_OUTPUT, 'production_aliases=' + aliases + '\n');
          "

      - name: Create the staged production deployment
        id: deploy
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          output=$(vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod --yes --token "$VERCEL_TOKEN" 2>&1) || {
            printf '%s\n' "$output"
            exit 1
          }
          printf '%s\n' "$output"
          url=$(printf '%s' "$output" \
            | grep -Eo 'https://[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.vercel\.app' \
            | grep -vx 'https://zes-builder.vercel.app' \
            | head -n 1 || true)
          if [ -z "$url" ]; then
            echo "::error::the staged deployment URL could not be parsed from the CLI output"
            exit 1
          fi
          id=$(printf '%s' "$output" | grep -Eo 'dpl_[A-Za-z0-9]{25}' | head -n 1 || true)
          if [ -n "$id" ]; then
            echo "id=$id" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
          fi
          echo "url=$url" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
          echo "staged deployment URL: $url"

      - name: Wait for READY and capture the deployment id
        id: ready
        env:
          DEPLOY_URL: ${{ steps.deploy.outputs.url }}
          DEPLOYMENT_ID: ${{ steps.deploy.outputs.id }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          node --input-type=module -e "
            const projectId = process.env.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID;
            const headers = { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + process.env.VERCEL_TOKEN };
            const deployUrl = process.env.DEPLOY_URL;

            let deploymentId = process.env.DEPLOYMENT_ID || null;
            const listResponse = await fetch('https://api.vercel.com/v6/deployments?projectId=' + projectId + '&limit=10', { headers });
            if (!deploymentId && listResponse.ok) {
              const list = await listResponse.json();
              const match = (list.deployments ?? []).find((entry) => entry.url && deployUrl.endsWith(entry.url));
              if (match) {
                deploymentId = match.id;
              }
            }
            if (!deploymentId) {
              console.error('the staged deployment could not be resolved to a deployment id');
              process.exit(1);
            }

            const deadline = Date.now() + 15 * 60 * 1000;
            let deployment = null;
            while (Date.now() < deadline) {
              const response = await fetch('https://api.vercel.com/v13/deployments/' + deploymentId, { headers });
              if (response.ok) {
                deployment = await response.json();
                if (deployment.readyState === 'READY' || deployment.readyState === 'ERROR') {
                  break;
                }
              }
              await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 5000));
            }

            if (!deployment || deployment.readyState !== 'READY') {
              console.error('the staged deployment never reached READY: ' + (deployment?.readyState ?? 'unknown'));
              process.exit(1);
            }

            const aliases = deployment.alias ?? [];
            console.log('deployment id: ' + deployment.id);
            console.log('ready state: ' + deployment.readyState);
            console.log('aliases: ' + (aliases.join(',') || 'none'));
            console.log('target: ' + (deployment.target ?? 'unknown'));

            if (aliases.includes(process.env.PRODUCTION_DOMAIN)) {
              console.error('the staged deployment already holds ' + process.env.PRODUCTION_DOMAIN + '; stopping');
              process.exit(1);
            }

            const fs = await import('node:fs');
            fs.appendFileSync(process.env.GITHUB_OUTPUT, 'deployment_id=' + deployment.id + '\n');
            fs.appendFileSync(process.env.GITHUB_OUTPUT, 'deployment_url=' + deployUrl + '\n');
          "

      - name: Verify that production was not touched
        env:
          DEPLOYMENT_ID: ${{ steps.ready.outputs.deployment_id }}
          PRODUCTION_ID_BEFORE: ${{ steps.before.outputs.production_id }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          node --input-type=module -e "
            const headers = { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + process.env.VERCEL_TOKEN };
            const response = await fetch('https://api.vercel.com/v9/projects/' + process.env.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID, { headers });
            const project = await response.json();
            const production = project.targets?.production ?? {};
            const aliases = production.alias ?? [];
            console.log('production deployment after the staged deployment: ' + production.id);
            console.log('production aliases after the staged deployment: ' + aliases.join(','));
            if (production.id !== process.env.PRODUCTION_ID_BEFORE) {
              console.error('the current production deployment changed: ' + process.env.PRODUCTION_ID_BEFORE + ' -> ' + production.id);
              process.exit(1);
            }
            if (!aliases.includes(process.env.PRODUCTION_DOMAIN)) {
              console.error(process.env.PRODUCTION_DOMAIN + ' is no longer assigned to the current production deployment');
              process.exit(1);
            }
            if ((production.alias ?? []).includes(process.env.DEPLOYMENT_ID)) {
              console.error('the staged deployment became the current production deployment');
              process.exit(1);
            }
          "

      - name: Health and smoke checks against the staged deployment URL
        env:
          DEPLOY_URL: ${{ steps.deploy.outputs.url }}
          VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          bypass="${VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET:-}"
          if [ -z "$bypass" ] && [ -f .env.production.local ]; then
            bypass=$(grep -E '^VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET=' .env.production.local | head -n 1 | cut -d= -f2- || true)
          fi

          check() {
            local path="$1"
            local expected="$2"
            local body="/tmp/smoke$(printf '%s' "$path" | tr '/.' '__')"
            local code
            code=$(curl -sS -o "$body" -w '%{http_code}' --max-time 30 "$DEPLOY_URL$path" || true)
            if [ "$code" = "302" ] || [ "$code" = "401" ] || [ "$code" = "403" ]; then
              if [ -n "$bypass" ]; then
                code=$(curl -sS -o "$body" -w '%{http_code}' --max-time 30 \
                  -H "x-vercel-protection-bypass: $bypass" "$DEPLOY_URL$path" || true)
              else
                echo "::error::the staged deployment URL is protected by Vercel Deployment Protection and no VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET was found in the production environment; approve C-5b before the first release"
                exit 1
              fi
            fi
            echo "$path -> $code"
            if [ "$code" != "$expected" ]; then
              echo "::error::smoke check failed for $path (expected $expected, got $code)"
              exit 1
            fi
          }

          check / 200
          check /api/health 200
          check /api/websites 401

          if ! grep -q '"status":"healthy"' /tmp/smoke_api_health 2>/dev/null; then
            echo "::error::the health endpoint did not report a healthy status"
            exit 1
          fi

          rm -f /tmp/smoke__ /tmp/smoke_api_health /tmp/smoke_api_websites

      - name: Remove the pulled environment file
        if: always()
        run: rm -f .env.production.local .env.production

      - name: Staged deployment summary
        env:
          DEPLOYMENT_ID: ${{ steps.ready.outputs.deployment_id }}
          DEPLOYMENT_URL: ${{ steps.ready.outputs.deployment_url }}
          SHA: ${{ needs.validate.outputs.sha }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          {
            echo "STAGED PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT READY"
            echo ""
            echo "Deployment ID: ${DEPLOYMENT_ID}"
            echo "Deployment URL: ${DEPLOYMENT_URL}"
            echo "Commit SHA: ${SHA}"
            echo ""
            echo "Automated validation: PASSED"
            echo "Deployment readiness: READY"
            echo "Health check: PASSED"
            echo ""
            echo "Production promotion: NOT PERFORMED"
            echo ""
            echo "Next action:"
            echo "The owner must inspect the staged deployment and manually promote"
            echo "it through the Vercel Dashboard."
          } >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
          {
            echo "STAGED PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT READY"
            echo "Deployment ID: ${DEPLOYMENT_ID}"
            echo "Deployment URL: ${DEPLOYMENT_URL}"
            echo "Commit SHA: ${SHA}"
            echo "Automated validation: PASSED"
            echo "Deployment readiness: READY"
            echo "Health check: PASSED"
            echo "Production promotion: NOT PERFORMED"
            echo "Next action:"
            echo "The owner must inspect the staged deployment and manually promote"
            echo "it through the Vercel Dashboard."
          } | tee -a "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
